# Firmware the live system needs to show a screen and reach the network on common
# laptops: the free blobs, the shared non-free set and the wifi and graphics families.
# Not the firmware-linux metapackage, and not live-build's own firmware detection
# (--firmware-chroot, off in auto/config): either pulls the firmware for data-centre
# network cards and the like, which alone pushes the image past a gigabyte. The installed
# system gets the full set from Debian's mirrors (modules/packages.conf). All of this
# is from Debian's non-free-firmware area: the same blobs every base ships, and the only
# non-free content in the image (README, "The stance").
firmware-linux-free
firmware-misc-nonfree
firmware-intel-graphics
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-realtek
firmware-atheros
firmware-brcm80211
firmware-mediatek
